            <ArticleTitle>[A female runner with a painful knee].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A9775</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 36-year-old, healthy woman presented with pain in her left knee. The X-ray of this knee showed a lytic tumour. The MRI scan also revealed this lesion, which was highly suspicious for a giant cell tumour of the distal femur. She was treated in a specialised centre.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
